          "path": "_m/r/p/4/h/lorentz-national-park-wp/the-pyramids-of-the-equator.jpg",
          "filename": "The Pyramids of the Equator.jpg",
          "caption": "The photo is taken from a viewing point of the Grasberg Mine. On this rare sunny day on top of the mountains, you can see the tallest mountain in the oceanic region, Carstensz Pyramid, or now known as Puncak Jaya. The mountain has many names, but the locals call it nemangkawi, which means the holy arrow. it represents the peace between the many tribes that live in the surrounding area",
